256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 108 0 R
/T (The most time-sensitive source is the phone itself. Phones that have location services enabled and are using the app send anonymised location and speed information, which, when combined across many devices on the same road, shows how fast traffic is actually moving. Individually these signals are small; in aggregate they form a continuous high-velocity stream, which is why this source drives the velocity characteristic in Table 2.1.)
/E (The most time-sensitive source is the phone itself. Phones that have location services enabled and are using the app send anonymised location and speed information, which, when combined across many devices on the same road, shows how fast traffic is actually moving. Individually these signals are small; in aggregate they form a continuous high-velocity stream, which is why this source drives the velocity characteristic in Table 2.1.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
