/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 111 0 R
/T (Mapping Google Maps showed that a big data system is a chain in which each stage depends on the others: sources decide what can be known, storage decides how quickly it can be retrieved, processing decides how useful it becomes, and output decides whether users keep generating new data. The feedback loop is the defining feature, because the product improves as people use it. The same loop is the reason for the governance controls in Figure 2.2, since every improvement in accuracy is paid for with data about people. The next module follows the machine learning part of such a pipeline in detail.)
/E (Mapping Google Maps showed that a big data system is a chain in which each stage depends on the others: sources decide what can be known, storage decides how quickly it can be retrieved, processing decides how useful it becomes, and output decides whether users keep generating new data. The feedback loop is the defining feature, because the product improves as people use it. The same loop is the reason for the governance controls in Figure 2.2, since every improvement in accuracy is paid for with data about people. The next module follows the machine learning part of such a pipeline in detail.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
