/T (every step rather than on the algorithm alone. To show the whole sequence the group selected a small project that can be completed from start to finish: classifying iris flowers into three species from four measurements. The dataset was published by the statistician R. A. Fisher in 1936 and is distributed with the scikit-learn library. It is far cleaner than real business data, so the results below should be read as a demonstration of the process and not as a claim about difficult problems. All numbers in this module were produced by running the code on this dataset, with a fixed random seed so that they can be reproduced.)
