/T (parts: 40 training samples and 10 test samples per species. The test set is then locked away. Scaling puts all measurements on a similar range, which matters for distance-based methods and for logistic regression, and the scaling values are calculated from the training set only. Calculating them on the full dataset would let information from the test samples leak into training and make the final result look better than it should. This kind of leakage is one of the most common mistakes in real projects.)
