/T (In a deployed system the trained model and its scaling values would be saved together and exposed through a service that receives measurements and returns a species with a probability. After deployment the project continues: the distribution of incoming measurements is monitored for drift, a sample of predictions is checked against ground truth, and the model is retrained when performance falls. Table 3.5 lists common failure points and how this flow guards against each.)
