/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 117 0 R
/T (A neural network learns by adjusting its weights so that its output moves closer to the correct answer. Backpropagation is the procedure that tells each weight in which direction and by how much to change. It applies the chain rule of calculus to compute the gradient of the error with respect to every weight in a single backward sweep through the network, and it was popularised for multi-layer networks by Rumelhart, Hinton, and Williams in 1986. Together with gradient descent it is the training method behind nearly all modern deep learning models, including convolutional and recurrent networks.)
/E (A neural network learns by adjusting its weights so that its output moves closer to the correct answer. Backpropagation is the procedure that tells each weight in which direction and by how much to change. It applies the chain rule of calculus to compute the gradient of the error with respect to every weight in a single backward sweep through the network, and it was popularised for multi-layer networks by Rumelhart, Hinton, and Williams in 1986. Together with gradient descent it is the training method behind nearly all modern deep learning models, including convolutional and recurrent networks.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
