/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 119 0 R
/T (w11 was nudged up and down by 0.000001, the loss was recalculated each time, and the slope was estimated from the two results. The estimate was -0.0036537, which agrees with the backpropagation value of -0.0036537 to all digits shown, confirming the chain-rule derivation. Repeating the update step on the same example moves the loss steadily downward, as Figure 4.2 shows: 0.0439 at the start, 0.0226 after 10 iterations, 0.0062 after 50, and 0.0014 after 200, at which point the output is 0.947.)
/E (w11 was nudged up and down by 0.000001, the loss was recalculated each time, and the slope was estimated from the two results. The estimate was -0.0036537, which agrees with the backpropagation value of -0.0036537 to all digits shown, confirming the chain-rule derivation. Repeating the update step on the same example moves the loss steadily downward, as Figure 4.2 shows: 0.0439 at the start, 0.0226 after 10 iterations, 0.0062 after 50, and 0.0014 after 200, at which point the output is 0.947.)
/Pg 24 0 R
