/T (and trimming spaces. The intent matcher tests the cleaned text against a list of patterns in order, and the first match decides the intent. A small context memory stores what the bot asked or offered in the previous turn, so that a short reply such as 'yes' or 'canteen' can be understood. Finally a template reply is returned, or a fallback message if nothing matched.)
