/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 125 0 R
/T (Module 2 mapped the flow of big data through a real system, from sources to output, with governance at each stage. Module 3 described the full machine learning workflow and demonstrated it with reproducible results. Module 4 opened the training step and worked through backpropagation with every number shown. Module 5 built a conversational program, the kind of system Turing's test imagined, and measured where its rules fail.)
/E (Module 2 mapped the flow of big data through a real system, from sources to output, with governance at each stage. Module 3 described the full machine learning workflow and demonstrated it with reproducible results. Module 4 opened the training step and worked through backpropagation with every number shown. Module 5 built a conversational program, the kind of system Turing's test imagined, and measured where its rules fail.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
837 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 125 0 R
/T (Future work could replace the hand-written rules of CampusBot with a classifier trained on collected student questions and evaluated with the methods of Module 3, connect it to real timetable data under proper consent and access controls, and extend the backpropagation example to a network trained on a real dataset. Taken together, the work shows that practical artificial intelligence depends on sound foundations, honest evaluation of results, and an understanding of the limits of every method used.)
/E (Future work could replace the hand-written rules of CampusBot with a classifier trained on collected student questions and evaluated with the methods of Module 3, connect it to real timetable data under proper consent and access controls, and extend the backpropagation example to a network trained on a real dataset. Taken together, the work shows that practical artificial intelligence depends on sound foundations, honest evaluation of results, and an understanding of the limits of every method used.)
