/Title (thebasepictureof land, buildings, and roads. Camerason vehiclesand on portableequipmentcapture street-level imagery for Street View. Authoritative datasets from governments, transport agencies, and commercial providers supply road networks, speed limits, addresses, and public-transport timetables; the common timetable format used by transit agencies, GTFS, was in fact created by Google together with a transit agency. Business owners and ordinary users add place names, opening hours, photographs, reviews, and corrections.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1636 0 R
/Next 1740 0 R
>>
endobj
1740 0 obj
<<
/Title (The most time-sensitive source is the phone itself. Phones that have location services enabled and are using the app send anonymised location and speed information, which, when combined across many devices on the same road, shows how fast traffic is actually moving. Individually these signals are small; in aggregate they form a continuous high-velocity stream, which is why this source drives the velocity characteristic in Table 2.1.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1636 0 R
/Prev 1739 0 R
>>
