/Title (Incoming data is separated by its nature. Live signals pass through a streaming ingestion layer that handles a constant flow of small events. Imagery and map files are loaded in batches into large distributed object storage, where files are replicated across machines so that the loss of a single disk or server does not lose data. Geographic information is held in spatial databases and indexed by area, so that a request for one neighbourhood can be answered without scanning the world. Map data is served in small square tiles at different zoom levels, so a phone downloads only what it needs for the current view. Historical traffic is archived because patterns repeat by hour and day of week, and that history later improves predictions.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1766 0 R
/First 1812 0 R
/Last 1813 0 R
/Count -2
>>
