1835 0 obj
<<
/Title (In streaming mode, location signals are matched to roads and combined into live speed estimates. The road network is represented as a graph, with junctions as nodes and road segments as weighted edges, and route finding is a shortest-path search on that graph using algorithms of the Dijkstra and A* family with acceleration techniques for continental-scale networks. Google researchers have also described using graph neural networks to predict the time needed to travel along road segments, which improves arrival-time estimates by learning from historical and live traffic together. This is a direct use of the machine learning methods discussed in Modules 3 and 4.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1815 0 R
/Prev 1834 0 R
>>
endobj
