/Title (is as important as engineering. The principles of informed consent, purpose limitation, and data minimisation apply directly to this kind of data. Figure 2.2 places the main controls at each stage. They include opt-in collection with clear prompts, controls that let users pause or delete their location history, anonymisation and aggregation before data is used for traffic, blurring of faces and number plates, and limits on what external developers can obtain through the API. In India the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 adds requirements of lawful consent and purpose limitation for processing of personal data.)
