/Title (Each candidate was trained on the 120 training samples. To compare them without touching the test set, the group used stratified 5-fold cross-validation: the training data is split into five parts, the model is trained on four and checked on the fifth, and this is repeated so that every part is used once for checking. The average of the five scores is a more stable estimate than a single split. All three models obtained the same mean cross-validation accuracy of 95.8 per cent, with a standard deviation of 2.6 percentage points across folds, as shown in Table 3.4 and Figure 3.2.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
